{
 "format": "snug conformance corpus v1. Each suite: cddl text, profile (full unless stated), cases [{rule, hex, expect: true|false, reason?, note?}]. A suite with schemaError expects compile to fail with that code. phase:\"later\" suites are not yet gated.",
 "source": "P8.2 regression vectors for the 2026-11-04 audit (docs/conformance.md S15, S16, S32, S60-S62, D038, D121). Expected verdicts are the RFC verdicts (RFC 8610 §3.8.6 and §3.9, RFC 8949 §3.4.1, §3.4.2 and §3.4.5.3, RFC 3339 §5.6-§5.7, RFC 3986 URI-reference); every case was also run on 2026-11-04 through the Ruby cddl gem 0.12.14 (`schema.cddl validate data.cbor`) and the offline-rebuilt Rust cddl 0.10.7 CLI (`--ci validate`). A note records each disagreement; where a reference tool and the RFC disagree the RFC verdict is kept.",
 "notes": [
  "Ruby validates the FIRST rule of a schema; every schema here starts with r.",
  "Ruby 0.12.14 refuses every tag-0 time with second 60, including real leap seconds (2016-12-31T23:59:60Z) and RFC 3339 §5.7's own example; RFC 3339 admits them (D252).",
  "Neither reference checks tag-32 URI syntax or tag-0 offsets/leap seconds structurally; their acceptances there are not evidence of validity.",
  "Rust 0.10.7 refuses NaN for float .ne 1.5 and mishandles controls on bounded float ranges and .and; the audit already recorded the first as a shared bug.",
  "Every suite runs under the deterministic wire preset (options.wire, D120-D125, any tag per D180; vm-test passes its profile flags): scalar -0.0, infinities and NaN appear only as float16 (D122). The Bindle preset would refuse them before the schema."
 ],
